{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Remediation Cycle",
  "description": "When a closure report is renamed to _REMEDIATE.md (UNSTABLE verdict), create a baseline copy of current test cases, generate/update REMEDIATION_LOG.md, and produce updated test cases for the next iteration.",
  "version": "3",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "**/4_Reviewer/FINAL_CLOSURE_REPORT_*_REMEDIATE.md"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A closure report was marked for remediation (UNSTABLE verdict). You are acting as the QA-Evidence-Reviewer-Agent for failure analysis and QA-Validator-Agent for test case updates. Follow @context_efficiency.md rules throughout.\n\nSTEP 1 — DETERMINE ITERATION NUMBER:\nCheck if REMEDIATION_LOG.md exists in the ticket root folder.\n- If it does NOT exist: this is iteration R1 (first remediation cycle).\n- If it DOES exist: read it, find the highest iteration number, and increment by 1.\n\nSTEP 2 — BASELINE COPY:\nCopy the current FINAL_TEST_CASES_*_API.md (or _OK.md) from 2_Validator/ to 5_Snapshots/FINAL_TEST_CASES_*_BASELINE_R{N}.md where {N} is the iteration number from Step 1. This preserves the test cases as they were before remediation modifies them.\n\nSTEP 3 — ANALYZE FAILURES:\nUse the @EvidenceAuditAnalyzer.md skill to read the EXECUTION_FINDINGS_*.md from 4_Reviewer/ and identify:\n- Which test cases (TC IDs) had FAIL or BLOCKED results\n- The root cause or observation for each failure\n- Any patterns across failures (e.g., same API endpoint, same entity type)\nRead @evidence_standards.md for verdict logic rules.\n\nSTEP 4 — UPDATE REMEDIATION LOG:\nCreate or append to REMEDIATION_LOG.md in the ticket root with:\n- Iteration number (R1, R2, etc.)\n- Timestamp\n- Failed TC IDs and their failure reasons (from EXECUTION_FINDINGS)\n- Actions to be taken (test case updates, new test cases, removed test cases)\n- Status: IN_PROGRESS\n\nFormat:\n```\n## Iteration R{N} — {timestamp}\n| TC ID | Verdict | Failure Reason | Action |\n|-------|---------|----------------|--------|\n| TC-XX | FAIL    | {reason}       | {action} |\n\nStatus: IN_PROGRESS\n```\n\nSTEP 5 — UPDATE TEST CASES:\nRead the current FINAL_TEST_CASES from 2_Validator/. Read @TestCasesDesign.md for formatting standards. Use the @TestCaseStandardizer.md skill to ensure all test cases conform to the required format. Based on the failure analysis:\n- Adjust expected results for test cases where the expectation was wrong\n- Add new test cases if failures revealed untested scenarios\n- Mark test cases for removal if they are no longer applicable\n- Do NOT remove passing test cases\nIMPORTANT — Output rules: If a FINAL_TEST_CASES_{TICKET_ID}_PENDING.md already exists in 2_Validator/, you MUST overwrite it (not create a second file). Use a single fsWrite call to write the complete file content in one operation — do NOT split across fsWrite + fsAppend. Save the updated test cases as 2_Validator/FINAL_TEST_CASES_{TICKET_ID}_PENDING.md for human review. Write only to 2_Validator/ and ticket root.\n\nSTEP 6 — STOP:\nStop after saving. The human will review the updated test cases, re-execute tests, drop new evidence, and re-trigger the reviewer via EVIDENCE_READY.md."
  }
}